From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: egret <noreply@egret.local>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:46:28 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Check a Paimon base-table policy for its system tables

A Paimon system table (t$files, t$snapshots, t$partitions, ...) is a PaimonTable, not a
MetadataTable, so patch 0001's refuse-under-policy check never reaches it. Refuse it to a
user whom a row access or column masking policy on the base table applies to, reusing 0001's
isRestrictedByPolicy and ERR_ACCESS_DENIED_METADATA_TABLE_UNDER_POLICY. No base-SELECT check:
Paimon system tables are already authorised by name.
---
 .../authorization/ColumnPrivilege.java        |  34 ++++
 .../ColumnPrivilegePaimonSystemTableTest.java | 172 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 206 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 fe/fe-core/src/test/java/com/starrocks/authorization/ColumnPrivilegePaimonSystemTableTest.java

diff --git a/fe/fe-core/src/main/java/com/starrocks/authorization/ColumnPrivilege.java b/fe/fe-core/src/main/java/com/starrocks/authorization/ColumnPrivilege.java
